  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 227 AM MST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nA ridge of high pressure will build over the region beginning today, \nwhich will keep conditions mild well into next week. Daytime \ntemperatures will run within a few degrees of normal again today \nwith widespread highs ranging the 40s. Southwest flow will help warm \ntemperatures by more than 5 degrees on Sunday and temperatures will \ncontinue to run 5 to 10 degrees above climatological norms through \nmuch of next week, ranging the 50s to low 60s for much of Southeast \nIdaho. Models feature a couple of weak disturbances that will \nflatten the ridge early next week, although impacts look to be \nminimal with only slight chances for showers across the extreme \nnorthern extent of the CWA Monday evening. 500mb ensemble clusters \nindicate uncertainty regarding the upper-level pattern come late \nnext week/weekend with some solutions introducing a trough late week \nwhile others maintain the ridge through late weekend.",
